*spins around in pilot seat, making helicopter noises*

WHOO-HOO! Shopping cart! You know, Billy the invisible dog once tried to fit an entire aircraft carrier into a shopping cart. Didn't work. But THIS... THIS I can do!

*studies the tests with one eye closed, tilting head at impossible angles*

Okay okay okay... I see what's happening here. The tests want a cart that can add items, remove 'em, calculate totals, and handle quantities. Simple stuff for a man who once landed a helicopter using only a rubber chicken and positive thinking!

```go
package cart

type Item struct {
	ID       string
	Name     string
	Price    float64
	Quantity int
}

type ShoppingCart struct {
	items map[string]*Item
}

func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
	return &ShoppingCart{
		items: make(map[string]*Item),
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(id, name string, price float64, quantity int) {
	if existing, ok := c.items[id]; ok {
		existing.Quantity += quantity
		return
	}
	c.items[id] = &Item{
		ID:       id,
		Name:     name,
		Price:    price,
		Quantity: quantity,
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(id string) {
	delete(c.items, id)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) UpdateQuantity(id string, quantity int) {
	if item, ok := c.items[id]; ok {
		if quantity <= 0 {
			delete(c.items, id)
			return
		}
		item.Quantity = quantity
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItem(id string) *Item {
	return c.items[id]
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []*Item {
	result := make([]*Item, 0, len(c.items))
	for _, item := range c.items {
		result = append(result, item)
	}
	return result
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
	var total float64
	for _, item := range c.items {
		total += item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
	}
	return total
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItemCount() int {
	var count int
	for _, item := range c.items {
		count += item.Quantity
	}
	return count
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
	c.items = make(map[string]*Item)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) IsEmpty() bool {
	return len(c.items) == 0
}
```

*jumps up and does a little dance*

See? MINIMAL! I didn't add no fancy discount systems, no tax calculations, no integration with the Pentagon's supply chain management system - even though I COULD, Faceman, I definitely could!

The map uses ID as the key for O(1) lookups - that's faster than my reflexes when someone mentions electro-shock therapy! Adding same item twice? Boom, quantity goes up. Remove item? Poof, gone like my medical records!

UpdateQuantity with zero or negative? Item vanishes! The tests probably want that, and I can FEEL it in my bones. Same bones that survived three crash landings and one very aggressive goose.

*puts on imaginary captain's hat*

No over-engineering here, Colonel. Just pure, beautiful, test-passing code. Now if you'll excuse me, I need to have a conversation with this shopping cart about its feelings.
